1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,770
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,070
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,080
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:07,910
(Episode 61)

5
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:19,860
Mom!

6
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,140
Are you going somewhere?

7
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,340
I just have an appointment.

8
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:37,540
Want me to head down with you?

9
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:41,910
Why don't we grab a cup of tea
in my office instead?

10
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,780
Sounds good.

11
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,060
Mom?

12
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,400
Did I catch you off guard earlier?

13
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:05,340
I just really wanted to call you
"Mom" out loud for once.

14
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,470
But this is the office.

15
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,010
Even for an ordinary
mother and daughter,

16
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,880
addressing each other
by professional titles...

17
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:15,410
is basic courtesy to the employees.

18
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:18,420
Please be a bit more careful
from now on.

19
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:21,750
Did you really hate...

20
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:23,620
hearing me call you Mom?

21
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:27,530
It's not that I hated it.
It was just a bit unexpected.

22
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:32,330
Okay. I'll be more careful
from now on.

23
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:34,370
All right, thank you.

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,170
Still,

25
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:39,270
I don't know
when it might slip out again.

26
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:43,680
The urge to call you "Mom" wells up
so strongly in my chest,

27
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:44,940
it feels like it's going to burst.

28
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:51,680
I guess this comes
from a lack of affection, right?

29
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:55,090
You must have been so lonely.

30
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:56,520
Of course I was.

31
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,760
Deep in my heart,

32
00:01:58,790 --> 00:02:00,890
I've always longed
for my birth mother.

33
00:02:06,330 --> 00:02:07,800
Ko Eun Seol...

34
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,540
Is she messing with me?

35
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:21,550
Mom.

36
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:26,020
Why would Ko Eun Seol...

37
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:29,650
Why on earth is she calling
Director Joo "Mom?"

38
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,300
Did you need me for something?

39
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,670
Where have you been?

40
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:49,710
I was just reporting to Director Joo
about the scholarship foundation.

41
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,310
Is that so?

42
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:53,810
Yes.

43
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,160
I don't know.

44
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:13,060
I remember
walking down the street...

45
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:16,000
and somehow ending up
at the factory.

46
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:21,110
That's where I saw Hae Ra's dad.

47
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:22,540
Well, no.

48
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:24,540
After your father's accident,

49
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:27,650
I never ran into So Yeon
at the factory.

50
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:30,820
She must be getting things mixed up.

51
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:45,800
Sir.

52
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:47,270
Seok Jin!

53
00:03:48,330 --> 00:03:50,940
Look at you. How long has it been?

54
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,400
You've been doing well, right?

55
00:03:56,310 --> 00:03:58,180
I know this was
quite a long time ago,

56
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:00,140
but after my father passed away,

57
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:03,780
did my mother ever stop by
the factory on her own?

58
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:04,920
So Yeon?

59
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,120
- Yes.
- Let me think.

60
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:11,790
Right, she did come by once.

61
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:14,390
That day,
she looked so tense and rigid...

62
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,890
that it really startled me.

63
00:04:17,730 --> 00:04:18,930
She looked tense?

64
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:21,500
Yes. As if something
had frightened her deeply.

65
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:24,200
Her face was completely pale,

66
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,600
and she didn't answer
when I called her.

67
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,070
She just dashed off in a panic.

68
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:29,340
Seeing her stagger off like that
even made me anxious.

69
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,540
Are you certain...

70
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,480
it was really my mother you saw
at the factory?

71
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:35,210
Yes, I'm sure.

72
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,320
Not long after Seong Woo died,

73
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:41,120
something terrible happened
to So Yeon, too.

74
00:04:42,390 --> 00:04:43,990
I still regret...

75
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:48,090
not stopping her
and comforting her properly that day.

76
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:50,190
Where in the factory
did you see her?

77
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:52,030
Wait, it was...

78
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:54,970
By the offices.
Near Young Hoon's office.

79
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:58,070
His office was just around the corner
from where we worked.

80
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,410
Why did the CEO lie to me?

81
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:27,430
Chief Cha,
you should join our gathering.

82
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:29,930
- Your gathering?
- Yes.

83
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:33,540
There's a golf group
with the executives.

84
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:34,970
I already told them...

85
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:37,480
that I'd bring you along
starting this month.

86
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:39,710
Thank you, sir.

87
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,480
Take some lessons in advance, okay?

88
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:44,920
I'll arrange the schedule for you.

89
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,180
Understood, sir.

90
00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:48,390
Taking care of So Yeon is important,

91
00:05:48,690 --> 00:05:50,020
but for the sake of business,

92
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:53,490
you also need to build your network
ahead of time.

93
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,390
I'll help you,

94
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:58,530
so just follow my lead
step-by-step, Chief Cha.

95
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,470
Yes, sir.

96
00:06:02,030 --> 00:06:03,030
By the way,

97
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:05,740
did your mother mention
anything else?

98
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,440
I think my mother misremembered.

99
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,950
Of course she did.

100
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,080
If So Yeon says
anything else to you,

101
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:20,220
you can always ask me about it.

102
00:06:22,490 --> 00:06:24,860
Excuse me, Ms. Kang,
aren't you having lunch?

103
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:29,430
We're getting sushi today.
Would you like to join us?

104
00:06:30,630 --> 00:06:32,300
No, I'm not hungry.

105
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,500
See you later then.

106
00:06:47,510 --> 00:06:49,780
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

107
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,120
My daughter, have you had lunch?

108
00:07:00,490 --> 00:07:02,490
I told you not to call me first.

109
00:07:02,790 --> 00:07:03,960
Why so harsh?

110
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:06,200
Your dad just called out of worry.

111
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,470
Did my princess find out anything?

112
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:10,740
About the girl
you were switched with, I mean.

113
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:12,540
I told you I don't know.

114
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,540
Besides, I said she's dead.

115
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,510
Right, I see.

116
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:18,980
You really don't know anything
about her.

117
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,280
All right, get back to work then.

118
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:24,880
My head's already spinning as it is,
and now him too?

119
00:07:33,590 --> 00:07:35,030
You still don't know who it is?

120
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:37,860
Don't worry, Princess.

121
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:41,370
Your dad will get
to the bottom of it.

122
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,740
Off I go, then.

123
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:04,490
- Director Joo.
- Eun Seol.

124
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:08,560
- What should we eat today?
- Since it's...

125
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:10,730
Look at them
hanging out together again.

126
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,170
Mom, it's such a nice day today.

127
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:18,770
I think it feels even nicer
because I'm out with you.

128
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:27,750
Joo Ae Sook.

129
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,580
Who are you trying to fool
with that terrible acting?

130
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:32,220
You're obviously putting on a show.

131
00:08:38,290 --> 00:08:39,820
(Ko Eun Seol
on the Rehabilitation Scholarship)

132
00:08:45,730 --> 00:08:48,070
(Ko Eun Seol Was My Classmate)

133
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:51,940
"September 11, 2000."

134
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,580
Well, well.

135
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:04,850
My gut is never wrong.

136
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,020
It's you.

137
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,220
You're the one
who got switched with Hae Ra.

138
00:09:16,090 --> 00:09:18,230
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

139
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,770
Director Joo,

140
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:27,100
that underwear...

141
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:28,370
Where did you buy it?

142
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:34,450
It's a gift I got
from that friend back home.

143
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,820
I'm pretty sure
it was the same brand.

144
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:51,260
Hello.

145
00:09:51,930 --> 00:09:53,830
Is there a specific style
you're looking for?

146
00:09:54,070 --> 00:09:55,630
I'll just look around.

147
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:56,900
Sure.

148
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,210
It's a daring design,

149
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:11,750
but even middle-aged couples
often buy matching sets these days.

150
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:16,350
Just a few days ago, a gentleman
picked up a matching set too.

151
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,590
Would you like a closer look
at them?

152
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:33,400
It looks like Hae Ra will marry
sometime next year, doesn't it?

153
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,740
Since the CEO gave his blessing,

154
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:37,910
- most likely.
- The thing is,

155
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,440
the optics might be a bit awkward.

156
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:43,950
Chief Cha will be moving in soon,

157
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:46,250
and it feels inappropriate
for you...

158
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:49,290
to be the fifth wheel
between the two couples.

159
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:52,960
So I was thinking...

160
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:54,190
Director Joo,

161
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,130
maybe it's time you moved out.

162
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:00,530
I'd like to,
but every time I try to leave,

163
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:03,330
Hae Ra stops me
and insists that I stay.

164
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,870
Besides, once things get busy
with wedding preparations,

165
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:08,770
she'll need me a lot.

166
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:11,580
If that's the case, don't worry.

167
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,180
Hae Ra said so herself.

168
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:16,610
She said it's time to let you go.

169
00:11:17,950 --> 00:11:19,780
Hae Ra understands now...

170
00:11:20,250 --> 00:11:24,590
that she's been holding onto you
for far too long.

171
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,530
I understand.

172
00:11:27,890 --> 00:11:29,160
I'll think about it.

173
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:32,160
Right. I'll look into finding
a suitable place...

174
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,830
for you to stay.

175
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:44,040
Kim Jung Sun.

176
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:47,040
As if I'd actually leave.

177
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,510
If anyone's leaving, it's you.

178
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:00,760
It's me.

179
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,300
As soon as the article is ready,
please give me a call.

180
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,000
All right.

181
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Come in.

182
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:12,070
- Did you call for me, Mom?
- Yes, have a seat.

183
00:12:17,210 --> 00:12:19,180
You seem busy these days, Eun Seol.

184
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:22,880
Judging by your card statement,
you've been all over the place.

185
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,620
Is something going on?

186
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:25,820
Of course.

187
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,620
You gave me money to spend,

188
00:12:27,690 --> 00:12:29,090
so I wanted to make
every penny count.

189
00:12:29,490 --> 00:12:31,560
I went to see
the people I'm grateful to,

190
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:33,260
so I could thank them properly.

191
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:34,630
Aren't you proud of me?

192
00:12:34,930 --> 00:12:39,100
Right, well, you certainly have
a lot of people to thank.

193
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:41,430
Did you buy presents
for your family?

194
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:44,470
Yes, they were thrilled.

195
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:47,270
Right, good thinking.

196
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:50,640
Mom, I want to go shopping with you.
When are you free?

197
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:53,240
No matter how busy I am,
how could I not make time...

198
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,650
for my daughter?

199
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:58,780
(Reporter Do Ji Hoon)

200
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:06,720
Hey, I'll call you back later.

201
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:12,360
I don't mind you taking it.

202
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,800
No, it's nothing important.

203
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:25,480
(Reporter Do Ji Hoon:
This article will bury her.)

204
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:29,850
(Reporter Do Ji Hoon:
This article will bury her.)

205
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,300
What's the occasion, Hae Ra?

206
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:51,900
It's not like you to ask me
on a date.

207
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:55,710
No reason.

208
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:59,680
It felt like forever since we last
sat down for a meal together.

209
00:14:00,710 --> 00:14:03,550
We've both been so busy.

210
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:06,420
No matter how busy I am,

211
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:08,320
I'm always happy to make time...

212
00:14:08,390 --> 00:14:10,450
whenever my daughter
wants to see me.

213
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,390
Here you go.

214
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:17,860
Excuse me,
can I get this without eggs?

215
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:21,070
I'm allergic. Sorry for the trouble.

216
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:26,000
Eun Seol, can you not eat eggs?

217
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,870
I'm allergic to egg whites.

218
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:32,840
I haven't been able to eat them
since I was little.

219
00:14:32,910 --> 00:14:33,910
Oh my.

220
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,850
Me too.

221
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:38,180
I'm also allergic to egg whites,

222
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:41,150
so I haven't eaten eggs
since I was young.

223
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:45,060
We have quite a lot in common.

224
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:50,590
How is the scholarship program
going with Eun Seol?

225
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,400
She is being kind
and helpful, right?

226
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:00,900
Mom, what do you think...

227
00:15:01,810 --> 00:15:03,170
of Ko Eun Seol?

228
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:05,010
Eun Seol?

229
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:12,420
She's really hardworking
and has a big heart.

230
00:15:13,150 --> 00:15:16,450
By the way,
she recently cut her hair short.

231
00:15:17,090 --> 00:15:18,960
Looking at her like that,

232
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:22,660
she was the spitting image of me.

233
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:26,960
I had short hair like that
when I was young, too.

234
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,900
Fine, all right.

235
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,600
I'll accept it for now.

236
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:01,800
Accept what?

237
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:05,370
What are you accepting?

238
00:16:05,770 --> 00:16:07,400
You know, that thing.

239
00:16:07,470 --> 00:16:10,540
What you were talking about.

240
00:16:10,810 --> 00:16:11,810
That thing.

241
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:13,780
What did I say?

242
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:15,780
What are you talking about?

243
00:16:16,210 --> 00:16:18,020
You know what it is.

244
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:21,520
I'm saying
I'll accept your feelings for now.

245
00:16:23,950 --> 00:16:24,960
Really?

246
00:16:25,490 --> 00:16:26,490
You mean it?

247
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,790
You're saying
you'll marry me, right?

248
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:29,860
No.

249
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,470
First, you need to go get
your grandma's blessing.

250
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:36,730
It won't be easy,

251
00:16:36,970 --> 00:16:39,500
but having our elders' blessing
is how I want to begin.

252
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:42,240
You understand how I feel, right?

253
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,170
Yes. Sounds good, Ms. Seo.

254
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:45,940
I mean,

255
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:48,380
let's do that, Mi Rae.

256
00:16:49,250 --> 00:16:51,050
Why don't we ease into
speaking casually?

257
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:52,850
Should we?

258
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,420
My gosh.

259
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:10,930
Well, I'll always support
whoever you date.

260
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:14,170
- What?
- I'm just saying.

261
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,310
You'll always have my blessing.
Just know that.

262
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:18,480
Don't be like that
and just tell his grandma.

263
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:20,580
Tell her you want to date Eun Guk.

264
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:24,350
How long are you going to waste time
and exhaust your emotions?

265
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:27,080
It seems like Eun Guk
has feelings for you too.

266
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,390
Hyun Jae.

267
00:17:31,290 --> 00:17:33,190
Am I doing the right thing?

268
00:17:34,730 --> 00:17:37,130
You would have cheered me on
if you were here.

269
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:38,900
Right?

270
00:17:55,410 --> 00:17:56,780
Reporter Do Ji Hoon?

271
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,390
(Reporter Do Ji Hoon:
This article will bury her.)

272
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:11,730
She's definitely up to something.

273
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:22,440
Darn it.

274
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,510
What the heck?

275
00:18:26,210 --> 00:18:28,880
What... How did you get in here?

276
00:18:33,450 --> 00:18:37,020
How dare you hit my daughter?
Do you have any idea who you are?

277
00:18:37,650 --> 00:18:41,090
By the way,
she recently cut her hair short.

278
00:18:41,690 --> 00:18:43,630
Looking at her like that,

279
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:47,060
she was the spitting image of me.

280
00:18:49,870 --> 00:18:50,900
No.

281
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,370
That's impossible.

282
00:18:54,510 --> 00:18:56,110
There's no way it's Ko Eun Seol.

283
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:06,720
Secretary Choi.

284
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:11,790
You're also helping out with PR
for Cheongma right now, aren't you?

285
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:12,860
Yes.

286
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,360
Director Joo is overseeing
that department as well.

287
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:18,030
Do you know
a Reporter Do Ji Hoon, then?

288
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,630
Reporter Do Ji Hoon?

289
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,430
His name does ring a bell.

290
00:19:24,970 --> 00:19:25,970
Why do you ask?

291
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,370
Just curious.

292
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:29,870
Knowing a lot of reporters
will make it easier for us...

293
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:31,640
to promote the scholarship program.

294
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:33,040
That's true.

295
00:19:33,810 --> 00:19:34,810
Reporter Do Ji Hoon.

296
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,310
I'll look into him.

297
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:38,050
Thank you.

298
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:42,990
By the way, you seem a bit
different these days.

299
00:19:43,190 --> 00:19:46,160
You look like
you're bursting with energy.

300
00:19:46,490 --> 00:19:47,520
Really?

301
00:19:47,930 --> 00:19:49,860
Maybe it's because
I cut my hair short,

302
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:53,360
but people keep saying
I look just like Director Joo.

303
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:55,270
No.

304
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,170
You...

305
00:19:59,570 --> 00:20:00,900
and Director Joo are different.

306
00:20:02,770 --> 00:20:03,770
And...

307
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,780
you don't look like her at all.

308
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:09,450
All right. No need to be so serious.

309
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,380
Come on, let's go get lunch.

310
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:21,530
You're not like her at all.

311
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:23,660
And...

312
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,560
you shouldn't be.

313
00:20:30,470 --> 00:20:34,370
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

314
00:20:35,710 --> 00:20:38,040
Didn't you have lunch plans
with your friends today?

315
00:20:38,810 --> 00:20:41,810
Yes, but I'm not going. It's boring.

316
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:44,580
Sorry, today is my mom's day off
from daycare,

317
00:20:44,650 --> 00:20:46,120
and we already made plans
for pizza at home.

318
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:47,780
I want to come too.

319
00:20:49,650 --> 00:20:50,650
I'm coming with you.

320
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:54,320
All right then. Let's go.

321
00:20:58,030 --> 00:20:59,100
This is delicious.

322
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:01,130
- Is it good?
- Yes.

323
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:02,870
Here you go, Mr. Seok Jin.

324
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,140
Mom, come on.

325
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:07,600
You're the one who wanted pizza,
so eat up. Here.

326
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:11,880
I feel full just watching you eat.

327
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:13,780
Have plenty, Mr. Seok Jin.

328
00:21:17,210 --> 00:21:18,220
Mom, let me see you.

329
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,160
What's wrong, Hae Ra?

330
00:21:26,290 --> 00:21:28,260
Nothing.
I just got something in my eye.

331
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:30,330
Here.

332
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:31,760
Hae Ra,

333
00:21:32,230 --> 00:21:33,530
have some more.

334
00:21:34,430 --> 00:21:35,830
Eat a lot too, Hae Ra.

335
00:21:41,810 --> 00:21:44,910
Don't just sit there.
Go give her a hug.

336
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:46,840
Oh, right.

337
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:53,780
Hae Ra?

338
00:21:58,820 --> 00:21:59,820
Don't cry.

339
00:22:08,570 --> 00:22:11,270
- Don't cry.
- Don't cry, Hae Ra.

340
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:18,340
Come in.

341
00:22:21,310 --> 00:22:24,310
Dad, Grandma,
come out here for a second.

342
00:22:27,180 --> 00:22:28,190
What...

343
00:22:29,190 --> 00:22:31,250
What brings you here at this hour,
Teun Teun's mom?

344
00:22:32,660 --> 00:22:35,530
Mom, let's sit down first.

345
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:37,890
Join us. Have a seat.

346
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:44,570
Grandma, we have something
to tell you.

347
00:22:48,910 --> 00:22:51,780
We want to date officially,
with marriage in mind.

348
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:56,510
No, marriage would be much later.

349
00:22:57,780 --> 00:23:00,220
For now,
I'd just like to date Eun Guk,

350
00:23:01,420 --> 00:23:04,120
and I wanted to get
your permission first.

351
00:23:04,990 --> 00:23:07,260
Have a little shame.

352
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:10,660
No matter how tough
life has been for you,

353
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:13,300
you should still show
some good judgment.

354
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:16,500
Open your eyes
and take a good look around.

355
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:19,500
There are plenty
of good divorced people these days.

356
00:23:19,970 --> 00:23:22,010
- Grandma.
- Mom, come on.

357
00:23:22,010 --> 00:23:23,010
What?

358
00:23:23,210 --> 00:23:25,380
After all I've done raising you,
I can't even speak my mind?

359
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:28,250
Whether it's dating or marriage,
it's over my dead body.

360
00:23:28,810 --> 00:23:30,010
If you insist,

361
00:23:30,610 --> 00:23:33,980
just go throw this old woman out
somewhere.

362
00:23:35,050 --> 00:23:38,460
Know that it's completely
out of the question until then.

363
00:23:45,100 --> 00:23:47,630
Don't worry too much.

364
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:52,700
My mom was the exact same way
when she first met my wife.

365
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,570
- She was like that with Mom too?
- Yes.

366
00:23:55,610 --> 00:23:57,470
Now she's going to be laid up in bed
for a few days.

367
00:23:57,710 --> 00:23:59,010
There's a whole routine to this.

368
00:23:59,580 --> 00:24:02,480
Next, she'll go on a hunger strike.

369
00:24:02,910 --> 00:24:04,710
What if she collapses?

370
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:11,860
Like a squirrel hiding acorns,
I hide snacks all over the place,

371
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:13,960
and she finds and eats
every single one.

372
00:24:14,690 --> 00:24:16,430
Once, when her hunger strike ended,

373
00:24:16,530 --> 00:24:17,860
she came out 2kg heavier.

374
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,500
By the way,

375
00:24:23,730 --> 00:24:26,670
I already spoke to Director Joo
separately about this,

376
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:29,110
but I was thinking...

377
00:24:30,010 --> 00:24:32,940
of having her move out of our house.

378
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:37,380
What are you talking about?

379
00:24:37,910 --> 00:24:39,850
Hae Ra's getting married next year,

380
00:24:40,050 --> 00:24:41,620
and someone new will move in.

381
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:44,350
Wouldn't it be uncomfortable
if Director Joo stayed with us too?

382
00:24:44,650 --> 00:24:46,790
It'll be awkward for her as well.

383
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:50,430
You were the one
who kept her from leaving.

384
00:24:51,060 --> 00:24:55,670
She stayed in our home all this time
just to look after you and Hae Ra.

385
00:24:57,370 --> 00:24:58,740
Both Hae Ra and I...

386
00:24:59,370 --> 00:25:02,740
don't need Director Joo
looking out for us anymore.

387
00:25:05,110 --> 00:25:08,310
Why? Are you saying
you're the one who needs it?

388
00:25:08,550 --> 00:25:11,080
Come on, what are you talking about?

389
00:25:11,750 --> 00:25:13,750
So, what did Director Joo say?

390
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:16,450
- Did she agree?
- She said she'd think about it.

391
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:22,890
Besides, as the owner of this house,
if I'm uncomfortable with it,

392
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:24,590
what other choice does she have?

393
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:55,460
Didn't I tell you not to call?

394
00:25:56,090 --> 00:25:58,600
I got a gift for you, my daughter,

395
00:25:59,230 --> 00:26:01,130
and I was wondering
how to give it to you.

396
00:26:02,670 --> 00:26:03,670
A gift?

397
00:26:05,140 --> 00:26:06,200
What is it?

398
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,700
I'll tell you when we meet.

399
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,570
It's a surprise.

400
00:26:19,820 --> 00:26:22,150
(Actress K Accused of Verbal Abuse
and Forcing Staff to Run Errands)

401
00:26:27,790 --> 00:26:31,060
Is this why Eun Seol
was asking about Reporter Do?

402
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,800
Did she know Director Joo
would pull this?

403
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:40,970
Director Joo...

404
00:26:42,310 --> 00:26:44,510
Now you're targeting
the Chairman, too?

405
00:26:51,210 --> 00:26:54,020
Ms. Kim, this is Ko Eun Seol.
Where are you right now?

406
00:26:54,020 --> 00:26:55,220
Eun Seol.

407
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:59,620
Right now, reporters are swarming
outside the house,

408
00:26:59,690 --> 00:27:01,260
so I can't leave.

409
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:04,560
Of all days,
Hae Ra left early today, too.

410
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:07,560
I'll head over right now.
I'll call you once I get there.

411
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,800
Thank you, Eun Seol.

412
00:27:22,380 --> 00:27:23,580
What about these?

413
00:27:23,650 --> 00:27:26,650
My daughter is a bit slow
on the uptake, isn't she?

414
00:27:26,850 --> 00:27:28,590
I figured it out right away.

415
00:27:29,850 --> 00:27:31,020
Isn't it obvious?

416
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:32,720
She's that girl.

417
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:36,430
The one you were swapped with.

418
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:38,860
Ko Eun Seol.

419
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,500
Cheongma's hidden daughter.

420
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:52,610
So pick up my calls right away
from now on.

421
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:54,980
If you don't,

422
00:27:55,950 --> 00:27:58,050
I'll go meet Ko Eun Seol.

423
00:27:59,350 --> 00:28:02,720
Man, now that would be
a real surprise.

424
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:08,830
Do what your dad tells you, okay?

425
00:28:20,700 --> 00:28:22,570
(Who Is Cheongma's Ko Eun Seol
From the Viral Live Interview?)

426
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:13,360
Ko Eun Seol.

427
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:56,400
(A Trap Called Desire)

428
00:29:56,970 --> 00:30:00,900
Seeing you feels just like
looking at my younger self.

429
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:03,170
I was swapped with Ko Eun Seol?

430
00:30:03,440 --> 00:30:06,140
The daughter of Cheongma isn't me,
but Ko Eun Seol?

431
00:30:06,280 --> 00:30:08,280
Is it really okay
for you to tell me this?

432
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:10,280
Secretary Choi,
aren't you loyal to Director Joo?

433
00:30:10,310 --> 00:30:13,250
Did Ko Eun Seol happen to ask
about me, or anything like that?

434
00:30:13,250 --> 00:30:14,820
While we have the chance,

435
00:30:14,820 --> 00:30:16,290
let's handle the big stuff first.

436
00:30:16,290 --> 00:30:18,860
Let's sweep it all up
through nominee accounts.

437
00:30:18,920 --> 00:30:21,960
Did Cha Seok Jin
figure something out?

438
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:23,330
Care for a glass of whiskey?

439
00:30:23,330 --> 00:30:24,730
It makes my stomach turn.

440
00:30:24,730 --> 00:30:27,200
Were you behind this?
Why are you taking it this far?

441
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:28,830
Did you really have to
ruin everything like this?

442
00:30:29,670 --> 00:30:31,670
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
